    "intro_html":  "Madras is the hot one. It came out of South India by way of British curry houses, and what defines it is the combination of real heat with real acid, chili powder up front and lemon and lime at the back. This build marinates the chicken first, then simmers it with tomatoes, carrots and bell pepper and rounds the edge off with a single can of coconut milk. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
